(1, 1, "Fosfororganik birikmalar bilan zaharlanishda muskarinsimon belgilarni bartaraf etuvchi asosiy vosita qaysi?",
 ["Atropin", "Neostigmin", "Pilokarpin", "Fizostigmin", "Betanexol"],
 "In organophosphate poisoning, which drug reverses the muscarinic signs?",
 ["Atropine", "Neostigmine", "Pilocarpine", "Physostigmine", "Bethanechol"],
 "Atropin bilan birga xolinesteraza reaktivatori, talvasalarda esa diazepam beriladi.",
 "Atropine is given together with a cholinesterase reactivator, and diazepam for seizures."),
(1, 1, "Atropin bilan zaharlanishning antidoti qaysi?",
 ["Fizostigmin", "Pilokarpin", "Nalokson", "Flumazenil", "Pralidoksim"],
 "Which is the antidote for atropine poisoning?",
 ["Physostigmine", "Pilocarpine", "Naloxone", "Flumazenil", "Pralidoxime"],
 "Fizostigmin uchlamchi amin bo‘lgani uchun MNS ga o‘tadi va markaziy belgilarni ham bartaraf etadi; neostigmin faqat periferik ta’sir qiladi.",
 "Physostigmine is a tertiary amine, so it enters the CNS and also reverses the central signs; neostigmine acts only peripherally."),
(1, 1, "Miasteniyani uzoq davolashda qo‘llanadigan asosiy antixolinesteraza dori qaysi?",
 ["Piridostigmin", "Atropin", "Skopolamin", "Tropikamid", "Platifillin"],
 "Which anticholinesterase drug is the mainstay of long-term treatment of myasthenia gravis?",
 ["Pyridostigmine", "Atropine", "Scopolamine", "Tropicamide", "Platyphylline"],
 "Piridostigmin ta’siri 3–6 soat davom etadi, neostigmindan uzoqroq.",
 "Pyridostigmine acts for 3–6 hours, longer than neostigmine."),
(1, 1, "Dengiz kasalligining oldini olish uchun quloq orqasiga yopishtiriladigan plastir qaysi dorini saqlaydi?",
 ["Skopolamin", "Pilokarpin", "Neostigmin", "Ipratropiy", "Tiotropiy"],
 "Which drug is contained in the patch applied behind the ear to prevent motion sickness?",
 ["Scopolamine", "Pilocarpine", "Neostigmine", "Ipratropium", "Tiotropium"],
 "Skopolamin MNS ni tinchlantiradi; nojo‘ya ta’sirlari — uyquchanlik va og‘iz qurishi.",
 "Scopolamine calms the CNS; its side effects are drowsiness and dry mouth."),
